      "role": "user",
      "content": "Using bulk expression and clinical follow-up for 400 lung adenocarcinoma patients, I need a model that predicts each new patient's overall-survival risk, something like a penalized Cox model that outputs a risk score, which I can then lock and apply to an external validation cohort of 150 patients from another hospital without refitting. Ideally the score would also show which genes drive the risk."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"a model that predicts each new patient's overall-survival risk\" -- not available here as asked. NetZoo has no registered method or variant \"a penalized Cox model\". PANDA does not give it: one static network per set of samples; time points can only be compared as separate networks.\n2. \"apply to an external validation cohort of 150 patients from another hospital without refitting\" -- not available here: no registered workflow produces this. PANDA does not give it: one static network per set of samples; time points can only be compared as separate networks.\n3. \"the score would also show which genes drive the risk\" -- not available here: no registered workflow produces this. PANDA does not give it: one static network per set of samples; time points can only be compared as separate networks.\n\nNo registered workflow can give these as you asked them (above), so none is offered as asked.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
